"""Assemble the annual dataset, Switzerland 1998-2025, from the series transcribed from
the source APIs (retrieved 25-26 September 2026), and write data.csv (the input of
ssm_decomposition.py) and macro.csv (all series, used by make_tables.py and plot_figures.py).

Sources and series:
  World Bank, World Development Indicators (July 2026 vintage): NY.GDP.MKTP.KN, NE.CON.PRVT.KN,
    NE.CON.GOVT.KN, NE.GDI.FTOT.KN, NE.EXP.GNFS.KN, NE.IMP.GNFS.KN (constant LCU, 2020 prices);
    NY.GDP.DEFL.ZS; NY.GDP.MKTP.CN; SP.POP.TOTL; BN.CAB.XOKA.GD.ZS; goods and services balance
    from NE.RSB.GNFS.ZS; NE.EXP.GNFS.ZS; NE.IMP.GNFS.ZS; PX.REX.REER (2010 = 100); FP.CPI.TOTL.ZG;
    SM.POP.NETM.
  Eurostat: nasa_10_nf_tr (B9 net lending/net borrowing by sector S14_S15, S11, S12, S13, S2; P51G
    gross fixed capital formation by sector; D1 compensation of employees; CP_MNAC), nasa_10_ki
    (household gross saving rate), nama_10_lp_ulc (nominal unit labour cost growth), ilc_di11
    (S80/S20 income quintile share ratio).
  OECD Economic Outlook (annual): GAP (output gap), NLGQ (general government net lending, % GDP),
    NLGXQA (cyclically adjusted primary balance, % potential GDP), IRS (short-term interest rate).
  BIS, credit to the non-financial sector: total credit to households, % of GDP, Q4 (via FRED,
    QCHHAM770A).
  Penn World Table 10.01: labour share (via FRED, LABSHPCHA156NRUG).
"""
